{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNBrFJA1kzsubY54C7E6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EmXCPC29Y5Hp9BruQFPvGW","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"mkdir -p /tmp/e312 && cat > /tmp/e312/edit.py <<'EOF'\nimport re\np='/work/docs/proposal.md'\ns=open(p).read()\ndef rep(a,b):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(a)==1,a\n    s=s.replace(a,b)\nrep(\"a Kubernetes Lease in-cluster)\",\"`flock` in both modes; in-cluster the lock file is on the `-home` PVC, which is `ReadWriteOncePod`, with `replicas: 1` and the `Recreate` strategy)\")\nrep(\"a Lease lock in place of the `flock`\",\"the same `flock` on a `ReadWriteOncePod` volume\")\nrep(\"or node eviction under Kubernetes.\",\"or node eviction under Kubernetes (cause `evicted`, a transient one; `Status.Transient` and `closeout.CauseEvicted` arrive in later parts of #54).\")\nrep(\"| `Job` with an init container that shallow-clones the branch into an `emptyDir`; sidecar cloned by an init container (Phase 3) |\",\n\"| a bare Pod whose `pre` init container fetches the repo at `BaseSHA` with a per-job read-only installation token and runs the same `workspace` code as local `Prepare` into size-limited `emptyDir` volumes; the agent gets `work` with no `.git` |\")\nrep(\"| a pod from the role's `Dockerfile` image, or the default `ard-agent` image; hard timeout |\",\n\"| a bare Pod (no Job object): init `pre`, isolated `agent` container (default `ard-agent` image) under `ard job-exec`, plain container `post` that serves the result; hard timeout |\")\nrep(\"| pod phase plus container restarts |\",\"| the controller follows the agent's `pods/log` into the host log; log mtime |\")\nrep(\"| pod logs, committed to `.ard/<issue#>/logs/` at close-out |\",\"| followed into `~/.ard/logs/...` like local logs; stdout from the tee file `out/stdout` in the pulled result; committed to `.ard/<issue#>/logs/` at close-out |\")\nk='''Kubernetes-executor details (decided, design revision 3 of [#54](https://github.com/albertcbrown/ard/issues/54), recorded in [#312](https://github.com/albertcbrown/ard/issues/312); the work is split across later parts of #54, and #317 splits into the API layer and the executor). There is no job API on `ard serve`. **Pod shape.** `pre` fetches with the token passed through `http.extraheader` from the environment, never argv or `.git/config`; the git dir is on a `ctl` volume the agent does not mount; the role dir comes from `cfg.SHA`, so the k8s executor refuses a config without a SHA; sidecars are at pinned SHAs; the untrusted inputs and the scrub list travel in the per-job Secret, capped at 768 KiB (over the cap is a permanent failure with a named cause); `pre` copies the static `ard` binary. The `agent` container mounts only `work` and `out` and holds only its model credential via `secretKeyRef`: no GitHub token, no key, no Secret volume, no SA token. It tees stdout to `out/stdout`, enforces its own deadline, writes a done marker and reaps orphans as PID 1. `post` has its own pinned image and never runs a binary from a shared volume. It serves one route, `GET /v1/result`, on the pod IP, guarded by a preshared 32-byte `crypto/rand` key unique to the pod, mounted only in `post` and kept in memory by the controller, compared in constant time. It answers 409 until the agent has terminated and the marker exists, builds the tar in Go and never runs git, serves one request at a time, has header and idle timeouts, never logs Authorization, and exits 0 after the controller confirms or at the deadline. The transport is plain HTTP inside the cluster (the owner's choice): the key grants only this job's result, and a NetworkPolicy limits who can connect.\n\n**Controller.** `Prepare` builds the local workspace. It mints the read token, the key and the per-job Secret (owned by the Pod), and revokes the token (`DELETE /installation/token`) after `pre` terminates; tokens join the redaction set. Completion is decided only from the kubelet (`containerStatuses`, the agent's `state.terminated`), never from the agent-writable done marker. The controller then pulls the result and safe-untars it into `<id>.result`: it uses `os.Root`; accepts regular files, directories and symlinks, symlinks last; masks modes to 0644/0755; rejects hardlinks, devices, FIFOs, `..`, absolute paths, NUL, duplicates, any `.git` component and case-fold collisions; and caps compressed and decompressed bytes (counted on the stream), entry count, per-file size and gzip ratio. Close-out runs unchanged (`gitx.Snapshot` against `BaseSHA`). The exit code comes from the kubelet only and is saved in `<id>.done`; a pod that ends with no valid result is `Gone`, never `Exited` 0. Statuses: `Running`, `Orphaned`, `Exited`, `TimedOut`, `Gone`. The executor requires GitHub App auth, because a PAT cannot be scoped down. Keys are not persisted: after a restart the Reaper kills orphan pods, and a sweep by an `ard/repo` hash label finds pods with no state record. Handles of the other executor kind report `Gone`. Pod and job names are the lowercased id as `ard-<id>`, at most 63 characters, so ids over 59 are rejected. The client is a thin REST client over the in-cluster SA token behind an interface with a fake, with no client-go. The executor is not an effect: dry-run runs it as local jobs run today.\n\n**Layout and limits.** Pod paths are `/job`, `/work`, `/role`, `/sidecar`, `/ard-config`, `/ard-out` and `/ard-bin`; the result roots are `work/` and `out/`, and stdout is `out/stdout`, outside `work/`, so it never shows in `Snapshot.Changed`. Defaults: a 2 GiB `emptyDir` per pod, a result of 512 MiB compressed and 2 GiB unpacked, 200k files, 100 MiB per file, all overridable by `ard serve` flags. **Deadlines.** `h.Deadline = Start + Timeout`; the job-exec deadline is `h.Deadline - min(2m, Timeout/10)`; the pod's `activeDeadlineSeconds` is `Timeout + UploadGrace`, where `UploadGrace` is a 2 minute result-pull grace; the key is revoked at `Deadline` plus that grace; job-exec exits 124 at its deadline, which maps to `TimedOut`. **Settings and images.** Cluster settings (jobs namespace, images, sizes) are `ard serve` flags set by the chart, not `.ard/config.yaml`; `executor` is fixed at startup, and a later config with a different value is a config error until restart. The `ard-agent` image will be public under `ghcr.io/albertcbrown/ard` and holds no secrets (an image test checks it). It carries Go, jq, yq, osv-scanner, govulncheck and golangci-lint at the repo's pins but not trufflehog (AGPL). Roles with a `Dockerfile` use it until in-cluster builds exist.\n\n'''\nrep(\"**Agent CLIs plug in through adapters.**\",k+\"**Agent CLIs plug in through adapters.**\")\nrep(\"the Kubernetes `Job` gets a short TTL\",\"a Kubernetes job's pod and per-job Secret are deleted (no Job object, no TTL)\")\nrep(\"and the Kubernetes executor uses the default `ard-agent` image (agent CLIs, git, common linters).\",\"and under `executor: k8s` every role runs the default `ard-agent` image (agent CLIs, git, common linters) and a role `Dockerfile` is ignored until in-cluster builds exist. The starter scanners `cve`, `docs`, `error-codes`, `lint` and `missing-tests` use the tools in the public image; `trufflehog` roles stay off under k8s, and `ard config check` will warn (planned, later part).\")\nrep(\"executor: local              # local | k8s\\n\",\"executor: local              # local | k8s; fixed at startup\\n\")\ng='''in Kubernetes job egress is DNS and the internet minus private ranges and 169.254.169.254 (the #276 posture), and `pre` holds only a read-only per-job token revoked after it ends.\n- **Isolated agent pod.** The agent container holds only its model credential. `pre` and `post` run as a different UID. A ValidatingAdmissionPolicy enforces `shareProcessNamespace: false` and refuses the App Secret, hostPath, a Secret mount in the agent container and an agent `runAsUser` equal to the sidecars'.\n- **Result key and listener.** `post` serves one route, guarded by a per-pod 32-byte key mounted only in `post` and kept in memory by the controller, over plain HTTP (the key grants only this job's result, and ingress is limited). Ingress to job pods is allowed only from the ard-serve pod on the post port. `ard serve` has no listener or Service for this.\n- **Result untar is the boundary.** The controller treats the pulled tar as hostile: `os.Root`; no hardlinks, devices, FIFOs, `..`, absolute paths, NUL, duplicates, `.git` components or case-fold collisions; modes masked; byte, entry, size and ratio caps counted on the stream.\n- **Cluster.** The jobs namespace has Pod Security `restricted`; the job SA has no roles and no token; `enableServiceLinks: false`, non-root, drop ALL, RuntimeDefault seccomp, read-only root fs, `/tmp` on an emptyDir, `restartPolicy: Never`, images pinned by digest. The controller Role is namespaced: pods create/get/list/watch/delete, pods/log get, secrets create/delete, events list, no pods/exec.\n- **Residual risks (Kubernetes).** The model credential sits in a per-job Secret in etcd, so etcd encryption at rest is required. The tee'd stdout is agent-writable, so the agent can forge its usage figures, the same exposure as local Docker, accepted by the owner; the exit code still comes from the kubelet; revisit when split log streams are available. Pod egress reaches the whole internet, and a `network: false` pod still allows GitHub and model API CIDRs. Pod Security `restricted` relies on the cluster's admission.'''\nrep(\"in Kubernetes a network policy limits egress to the model API and package registries.\",g)\nrep(\"amended for the soak, [#144](https://github.com/albertcbrown/ard/issues/144)).** `ard serve` runs live\",\"amended for the soak, [#144](https://github.com/albertcbrown/ard/issues/144)).** `ard serve` runs live\") \ns=s.rstrip('\\n')+'''\n- [x] **Kubernetes executor ([#54](https://github.com/albertcbrown/ard/issues/54)).** Decided 2026-11-24, design revision 3 ([design comment](https://github.com/albertcbrown/ard/issues/54#issuecomment-7131825898), recorded in [#312](https://github.com/albertcbrown/ard/issues/312)): no job API on `ard serve`; the controller pulls the result from a `post` container with a per-pod key; plain HTTP inside the cluster; stdout from a tee file, with forgeable usage figures accepted as a risk; a public `ard-agent` image; cluster settings are flags, not config; `flock` on a `ReadWriteOncePod` volume; size defaults as in Kubernetes-executor details; trufflehog off under k8s. See Kubernetes-executor details and Guardrails.\n- [ ] **Redacting the preshared result key by value.** (#54) Not planned: the key is single-use and never in the agent container or the followed logs.\n- [ ] **Worktree registration after `<id>` is swapped for `<id>.result`.** (#54) Prune versus export tree is still open.\n'''\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\npython3 -I /tmp/e312/edit.py && cd /work && grep -n \"Lease\\|short TTL\\|job API\\|native sidecar\" docs/proposal.md | cut -c1-120; git diff --stat; (make lint test 2>&1 | tail -5)"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8639,"cache_read_input_tokens":17518,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8639},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a472646e-7b5e-4d9e-ad44-7952ed22203f","uuid":"f33c13e7-72c9-44c2-9eff-c153edfdcfb3","timestamp":"2026-11-24T17:59:29.087Z","request_id":"req_011ChNBrF9inM9fgJ7X9JPau"}
